course: dictionary
lesson: 7470
title: The porpoise: a sea mammal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A porpoise is a sea mammal, like a small dolphin. Look at its face and head: it has a short, round snout and a rounded head, not a long beak. «Porpoises are smaller cousins of dolphins with rounded heads, no long beak and spade-shaped teeth.» Those spade-shaped teeth are flat, like little shovels.
explain: Porpoises are not fish. They breathe air through a blowhole on the top of their head, they are warm-blooded, and mothers feed their babies milk. Animals that do all this are mammals, and porpoises belong to the same group as whales and dolphins, called cetaceans.
explain: Words can have more than one meaning, so use the context to choose. «The Mock Turtle says no wise fish would go anywhere without a «porpoise», which sounds like «purpose».» Here the word is a joke: porpoise and purpose sound alike, but only the animal is a sea mammal.
fact: A porpoise is a sea mammal, like a small dolphin.
fact: Porpoises have a short, round snout and a rounded head, with no long beak.
fact: Porpoises breathe air through a blowhole, are warm-blooded and feed their babies milk.
fact: The harbour porpoise lives around the coasts of Britain, Ireland and North America, and it is shy.
fact: The vaquita, a tiny porpoise in Mexico, is the most endangered sea mammal in the world, often caught in fishing nets.
exercise: «Porpoises are smaller cousins of dolphins with rounded heads, no long beak and spade-shaped teeth.» What shape is a porpoise's head? | Square like a box | *Rounded | Long and pointed like a beak | Flat like a fish's tail
exercise: Science says porpoises breathe air and feed their babies milk. What kind of animal are they? | A bird | A fish | *A mammal | An insect
exercise: «The harbour porpoise, which has a blunt face, not a beak.» What does blunt mean here? | Sharp and thin | Covered in long hair | Very long and curved | *Rounded, not pointed
test: «a pod of porpoises» means a group of porpoises. What is a pod? | A sharp tooth | A type of fish tail | A deep cave under the sea | *A group of animals
test: The vaquita is a tiny porpoise in Mexico. Why is it in danger? | *It is often caught in fishing nets | It has too many babies to feed | It is too big to swim | It lives on dry land
exam: «The harbour porpoise has a blunt face, not a beak.» Which picture fits a harbour porpoise best? | A long, pointed beak like a bird | *A short, rounded face | A flat, wide mouth like a frog | A long, thin snout full of spikes
